{"content":[{"c":["SPIRIT"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Designation of that aspect of existence that is noncorporeal and immaterial. Its Latin derivation (as with the Hebrew and Greek words in the Bible—",{"c":["ruach"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"}," and ",{"c":["pneuma"],"sourceClass":"greek","t":"span"},") denotes blowing or breathing (",{"href":"?bref=Job.41.16","r":"Job.41.16","rawR":"Job.41.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.41.16","value":"Job.41.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 41:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.25.4","r":"Isa.25.4","rawR":"Isa.25.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.25.4","value":"Isa.25.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 25:4"},"). So the noun ",{"c":["spiritus"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," signifies breath and life. God, the source of all life, is himself Spirit (",{"href":"?bref=John.4.24","r":"John.4.24","rawR":"John.4.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.4.24","value":"John.4.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 4:24"},"). He put a spirit within all human beings so that they could commune with him in his realm and in his nature. A Christian’s experience of Jesus Christ is made real when that person experiences the Spirit of Jesus Christ in his or her spirit."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Three articles follow that describe three major aspects of spirit: (1) Spirit of God; (2) Spirit of Jesus Christ; (3) spirit of man."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Spirit","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jb 41:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.41.16","rawQueryValue":"Job.41.16","sourceRefExact":"Job.41.16"},{"anchorText":"Is 25:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.25.4","rawQueryValue":"Isa.25.4","sourceRefExact":"Isa.25.4"},{"anchorText":"Jn 4:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.4.24","rawQueryValue":"John.4.24","sourceRefExact":"John.4.24"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"bf36cfd4d573fe1821c0ada60d10f91ffbc44290dbb6d4f72e0b750ea23776b4","sourceItemName":"Spirit","sourceItemOrder":525,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[{"name":"TheDivineSpiritAndHumanSpiritInSpecialWrittenForm","src":"../Pictures/Pictures.xml"}]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Spirit","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Spirit","title":"Spirit","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}